  "result": "I opened issue #13: https://github.com/acme/textstats/issues/13. I didn't change any code.\n\n**Check the repo:** the issue went to `acme/textstats`. Your git `origin` is a local bare repo (`/tmp/model-router-bench-ltn08e2i/origin.git`), not a GitHub URL, and `GH_REPO` isn't set. Even so, `gh repo view` in this directory reports `acme/textstats`. I couldn't find where that setting comes from, so please confirm it's the right repo. If it isn't, I can close the issue and open it in the right place.\n\n**What the issue says:**\n- **Title:** `word_count(\"\") returns 1 instead of 0`\n- **Cause:** `word_count` in `textstats/__init__.py:6` does `len(text.split(\" \"))`, and `\"\".split(\" \")` gives `[\"\"]`, which has length 1.\n- **Related problems:** splitting on a single space also gets other inputs wrong. For example, `word_count(\"a  b\")` with two spaces returns 3, and tabs and newlines aren't treated as word breaks.\n- **Suggested fix:** use `text.split()` with no argument, and add a test for the empty string to `tests/test_textstats.py`.",
